title: Case Manager › Active cases › Sort and page the tracker
route: /manager
intro: Six of the eight table headers sort. A second click on the same header flips the order. The table shows ten rows at a time with 'Previous' and 'Next'. Changing a sort or any filter always returns to page 1.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Tracker table is on screen\n(sorted by Next due, soonest first)"
screen h1 "Headers\nCase, Status, Next due, Units or days, Level of care, Payer, Approval chance, and a hidden 'Open' column\nSortable ones show an up-and-down arrow button 'Sort by ...'"
click c0 "Click 'Level of care' or the empty 'Open' header"
process p0 "Nothing happens: those two do not sort"
click c1 "Click a sortable header\n('Case', 'Status', 'Next due', 'Units or days', 'Payer', 'Approval chance')"
decision d1 "Is it the header already used for sorting?"
process p1 "Order flips: ascending becomes descending and back\nThe arrow points up or down"
decision d2 "Which header is it?"
process s1a "'Case': case ID, A to Z"
process s2a "'Payer': payer key A to Z (Beacon, Cardinal, Evergreen, Harborview, Lakeshore, Summit)"
process s3a "'Units or days': share of the approval used, lowest first\n'not yet approved' rows count as lowest"
process s4a "'Next due': soonest binding event first; overdue first of all\nA case that is also a request sorts by the case page's own due time"
process s5a "'Approval chance': highest first on the first click"
process s6a "'Status': Needs action, Review due, Awaiting payer, On track"
process p2 "Ties are broken by the soonest due time\nThe table goes back to page 1"

group gPage "Pager under the table"
  screen pg "'Showing 1 to 10 of 56'    'Previous'   'Page 1 of 6'   'Next'"
  click n1 "Click 'Next'"
  click n2 "Click 'Previous'"
  decision d3 "Is there another page that way?"
  process g1 "Next ten rows, text updates ('Showing 11 to 20 of 56', 'Page 2 of 6')"
  process g2 "Button is greyed out: 'Previous' on page 1, 'Next' on the last page"
endgroup
process p3 "The page count follows the filters: with fewer than eleven matches there is one page"
end e1 "Rows are in the new order"

s1 --> h1
h1 --> c0 --> p0
h1 --> c1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p1 --> p2
d1 -->|No: a new column| d2
d2 -->|Case| s1a --> p2
d2 -->|Payer| s2a --> p2
d2 -->|Units or days| s3a --> p2
d2 -->|Next due| s4a --> p2
d2 -->|Approval chance| s5a --> p2
d2 -->|Status| s6a --> p2
p2 --> e1
h1 --> pg
pg --> n1 --> d3
pg --> n2 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| g1 --> e1
d3 -->|No| g2
g2 -.-> p3
